# module Gradle vendored Maven integration

This adapter detects `settings.gradle.kts` before `settings.gradle` and consumes the ordinary
`maven` export name `group:artifact`. It applies only when the dependency has a locked vendor.

# decision Composite build substitution is generated by DSL variant

Kotlin consumers get `deps/git-a2a.settings.gradle.kts` plus one marked
`apply(from = "deps/git-a2a.settings.gradle.kts")` line. Groovy consumers get the analogous
`.gradle` file and `apply from:` line. Sorted dependency blocks use `includeBuild` and substitute
the export module coordinate with project `:`. Unwire removes only owned blocks and the marked
line when the generated file becomes empty.

The generated `deps/git-a2a.settings.gradle(.kts)` file is wholly tool-owned. Wire preserves
intact dependency blocks, discards every foreign byte with an explicit warning, and regenerates
canonical output; Drift reports foreign content and Unwire repairs or removes it without error.

# invariant Gradle and Maven share the maven export identity

`Ecosystem()` is `maven`; detection variant is `gradle-kts` or `gradle-groovy`. The later Maven
adapter shares the ecosystem but detects `pom.xml`, so a consumer activates only its own build
system while the dependency owner publishes one `group:artifact` identity.

# test Golden and real-toolchain lifecycle

Golden tests cover both DSLs, idempotence, drift, sorted blocks, and byte-restoring Unwire. The
opt-in integration matrix runs a real Gradle build against a copied vendored composite.
